adr: 0214
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: typeinquiry_field
why: `r.f` is the one spelling of a field-designator the parser cannot refuse, a variable-name admitting a qualifier (6.5.1) and the parser having no way to tell an imported interface from a record variable. So Sema asks the symbol. Without the question the lookup simply fails and the field is reported as an undeclared variable -- `unknown variable 'f' in 'type of'` -- which is a true sentence about a name that exists, pointing at neither the rule nor the record nor, since ADR-0215, at the mode that has the construct. The program is still refused, so only a golden holding the message itself can tell.
--- old
    if (q <> nil) and (q^.kind <> skInterface) then begin
--- new
    if false then begin
